WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.690
Let's Duel, Prince

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.410
<b>Trapped in</b>

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.750
<b>a Dating Sim</b>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.380
<b>Trapped in
a Dating Sim</b>

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.000
This is Marie's textbook.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.830
Her bag was burned, too.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.250
You really have no idea how this happened?

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.630
No, I don't.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:00.140
The girls present at the scene 
said you ordered them to do it.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.110
It wasn't me.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:04.390
Why won't you believe me?

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.700
Stay away from Marie.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.640
And us, too.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.440
Our engagement is an agreement 
made outside this school.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.900
Stay out of my business at the academy.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.660
Did you hear the news?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.660
A couple of the rich dudes 
have gotten engaged.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.720
Yeah. Not only that, but their partners are 
Milly and Jessica, who were nice to us, too.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.630
May you two find happiness, as well.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.790
How do you do?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.050
That just leaves girls with 
terrible personalities.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.430
It's over. It's all over for us.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.320
Leon, how are things with you?

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.930
I'm in the same boat.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.060
I'm sending out invitations to tea 
parties, but they just get ignored.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:56.070
By the way, it seems like Prince Julius 
is involved in some trouble these days.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:03:00.570
It's all the bullying that 
Marie girl is facing, right?

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.820
I heard the one at the center of the bullying

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.080
is the prince's fiancée and 
the duke's daughter, Angelica.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.830
The prince was furious 
when he heard about it.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.490
<i>The game also featured an event in 
which Julius got mad at Angelica.</i>

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.060
<i>But that's not supposed to 
happen until much later.</i>

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.720
Ms. Marie?

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.040
Yeah. I heard she's being bullied.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.150
I was wondering what she's actually like.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.430
I've only spoken with her once, but...

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.040
Mr. Leon, do you...

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:39.240
Do you like girls like Ms. Marie, too?

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.530
What?!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.530
What? You don't?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.870
Like her? I hate her.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.260
I see. When I spoke with her previously,

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.750
I saw her alone in the courtyard.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:57.250
I was curious, so I asked 
her if something happened.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.640
And then...

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.490
I hate girls like you.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.060
That's what she said to me.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.030
<i>"Girls like you"?</i>

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.520
<i>Something about that phrasing bothers me.</i>

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.090
H-Here?

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.480
Why not? We're alone.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.960
Mr. Leon, what are you doing?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:23.990
I'm curious.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.990
<i>Who gets together with who is a 
matter of life and death for us.</i>

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.500
You mustn't peep. It's indecent.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.000
Ms. Mari—

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.270
<i>I'm having so much fun.</i>

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.240
<i>Those dumb bitches have stopped bullying 
me since Julius got mad at them.</i>

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.840
<i>This world is the best.</i>

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:01.140
Marie.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.400
Your Highness! Jilk!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.160
Don't call me that. Julius is fine.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.740
All right.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.410
Marie, you don't have a 
personal servant, right?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.170
M-Money's a bit tight.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:22.130
Then the prince and I will pay for one.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.920
You must be lonely without a servant.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.500
Thank you!

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.430
<i>Lucky me. Now I'll have a 
handsome demi-human slave.</i>

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.430
I'll arrange for a carriage.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.950
<i>Normally it'd be insane for a woman to 
be openly accompanied by a paramour.</i>

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.440
<i>I'm gonna have so much fun 
in this otome game's world.</i>

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.200
This is unacceptable.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.450
You're not even allowed to have a slave.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.470
Leave it. The prince knows what it means 
for a woman to have a demi-human slave.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.060
That means that's all their relationship is.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.710
But...

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.240
I'm sorry. Could you leave me alone, please?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.550
You can't be serious!

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.470
<i>How dare he fall for that woman?</i>

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.490
<i>I was raised to serve my prince.</i>

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.000
<i>I've lived my life for only the prince.</i>

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:36.250
<i>I love the prince so much...</i>

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.470
So why?

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.040
Why?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.130
Hey, idiot!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:48.980
Oh, it's you, Jenna.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:49.880
Don't go back to sleep!

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.810
Do you know a girl named Marie?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.000
She's quite close with Prince Julius.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.390
Not just him,

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.400
but other boys, too.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.300
Did you hear about the duke's 
daughter bullying her?

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.320
You weren't involved, were you?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.250
I'm not involved in that.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.910
I heard the prince got mad at her.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.910
I'm sure her followers 
just acted on their own.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.230
Then I guess Ms. Angelica herself 
had nothing to do with it.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:30.670
In any case, you're not involved with the 
duke's daughter or the prince, right?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.680
No, I'm not. Is this really that important?

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.200
The prince will eventually 
succeed the throne.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.920
If you can get on his good side at 
the academy, you'll be set for life.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.470
And on the flip side, if you get 
on his bad side, it's over for you.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.160
I know that.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.450
You'd better not do anything 
dumb to embarrass me.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.790
The first semester is over already.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:04.440
All I got to do was host a tea 
party and visit a dungeon.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.530
You seemed to enjoy yourself, even if 
you're no closer to finding a wife.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.750
Do you have some kind of grudge against me?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.850
I despise new humans.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:16.410
In that regard, I dislike you, as well.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:20.520
You must be a pretty sad 
AI to be serving me, then.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.190
I'll be making you serve me your whole life. 
You'd best be prepared.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.980
I look forward to it.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.980
Hey, are you able to gather information?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.780
Concerning the duke's daughter 
and the girl named Marie?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.590
Yes.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.870
While it is possible,

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.740
I will not be telling you their bust, 
waist, and hip measurements.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.500
I do want to know 
Ms. Angelica's measurements.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.980
Too bad.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.660
Marie, why aren't you wearing a dress?

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:52.760
Um... I wasn't able to get one.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:58.260
I see. Well, you look far less stuffy 
than if you'd worn a luxurious dress.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.470
I'll take you to have a dress made sometime.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.520
Sure.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:10.360
Apparently, some nobles from the 
backwoods found girlfriends at this party.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.260
This is our chance!

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.280
Yeah!

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:15.270
A back country baron? No one asked for you.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.900
Don't come back until you've taken 
a look at yourself in a mirror.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.530
I'm looking for at least a viscount.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.710
Nobody likes a shallow man.

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:25.400
You're nothing like the 
prince and his friends.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.770
How insolent.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.070
U-Um, I—

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.040
If you'd just hear us out—

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.670
Daniel!

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.650
Lame.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.890
Come back once you've been 
reincarnated as better men.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.810
That's a good look for you, country boys.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.150
Damn it. Who the hell do they think they are?

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.670
I've had it with this.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.840
Girls are starting to make me feel sick.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.570
Mr. Leon, it's an emergency!

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.820
Why won't you understand?

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.970
I'm telling you this for 
your sake, Your Highness!

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.580
I can't stand to listen 
to what you have to say.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.380
That's all.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.830
What happened?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.330
Apparently Ms. Angelica saw 
Ms. Marie holding hands with a man

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.880
who wasn't the prince.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:19.340
Do you realize that woman 
is involved with all of you?

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.090
We know.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:26.100
She saved me by listening to my problems.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.900
This is why I wish to protect her.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.300
You try to rationalize everything too much.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.860
Just be honest and say you love her.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.610
Marie is a marvelous woman.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.610
It's only natural that I'd fall for her.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:45.990
You're right. But I believe 
I love her the most.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.320
No.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.630
<i>I</i> love Marie the most.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.150
Did you hear that?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.270
I'm so jealous!

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.130
I wish he'd say that about me!

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.890
You mean you won't let it end 
as a fling at the academy?

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.400
That's right. As far as I'm concerned, 
no one can replace her.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:12.930
It's only Marie for me.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.710
Is he calling off their engagement?

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.650
The duke's daughter is finished.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.920
How pitiful.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.040
Pick it up, foul wench 
who deceived the prince.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.300
A duel?

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.080
It's a duel.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:38.550
If she picks up the glove, 
it'll mean she accepts the duel.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.800
<i>The duel event...</i>

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:46.430
<i>In the game, the character with whom 
you had the highest relationship score</i>

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.700
<i>dueled in the protagonist's place.</i>

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.180
Pick it up, Marie.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.060
I shall be your champion.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.570
But...

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.070
<i>I expected this.</i>

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:02.920
I cannot allow Your Highness 
to hog the spotlight.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.570
I volunteer, as well.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.550
This sounds fun. I'm in, too.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:09.830
I'll take on any challengers.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.670
How dare you call her a foul wench?

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.080
I'm in, as well.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.300
I'm confident in my swordsmanship.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.340
I shall fight as Marie's blade.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.360
Guys...

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:26.720
I'm scared, but I'm relieved 
to have all of you.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.940
Don't forget about me.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.720
I can at least provide support.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.840
Thank you, Kyle.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:36.160
<i>Is this how girls feel when they see harems?</i>

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.960
<i>It gives me the creeps.</i>

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.240
What will the duke's daughter do now?

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.740
She's facing the prince.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.860
Nobody would want to fight him.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:48.870
P-Please, someone...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.630
Have you been abandoned by your followers?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:00.380
I have to feel sorry for someone 
with so little personal magnetism.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.850
<i>In the game, even if Ms. Angelica</i>

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.550
<i>appoints someone outside the 
academy as her champion,</i>

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:08.140
<i>if the protagonist wins, then ultimately...</i>

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.500
<i>She heads straight into ruin.</i>

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.520
<i>She marries a back country lord 
with a terrible personality</i>

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.050
<i>and lives a miserable life.</i>

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.940
How will she disgrace herself this time?

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.030
This'll end with her going 
crying back to her family.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:30.780
Angelica, I'm sure you're 
prepared to fight us.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.540
E-Even if I don't have a champion, I...

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.500
<i>Why do I feel like this?</i>

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.290
<i>It's not as though Ms. Angelica 
and I are close friends.</i>

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:44.550
<i>I want to be ordinary.
I just want to be a mob, but...</i>

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.300
Mr. Leon?

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:48.210
You...

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:49.180
What are you doing?

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:57.440
I really friggin' hate them.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:08.570
Okay, everyone. I volunteer 
to be her champion.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:09.650
Who is he?

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:10.470
Dunno.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.330
Some back country noble, right?

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:17.210
I heard someone succeeded as an 
adventurer prior to enrolling.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.710
Yeah, I've heard about that. 
Would that be you?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.060
Ms. Angelica, you need to 
appoint me your champion.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:27.540
What? Uh...

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.480
Just say you accept.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.850
I-I accept.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:42.230
Which means I, Leon Fou 
Bartfort, am her champion.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.990
The five of you will represent 
Ms. Marie, correct?

00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:51.740
Then I'd like to confirm the method 
of our duel, as well as the stakes.

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.240
<i>This girl...</i>

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.750
<i>I had Luxion look into her, 
and there's no mistaking it.</i>

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:01.210
<i>Like me, Marie isn't from this world.</i>

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.310
<i>She's been reincarnated, 
or something like it.</i>

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.290
By the way, Ms. Angelica, what demands 
do you have for your opponent?

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.880
Stay away from the prince.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.760
That's all I desire.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.680
Are you that desperate to keep us apart?

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.230
It's clear which of you is the foul wench.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.810
Yeah, could we skip all that tedious crap?

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:28.650
Hurry up and state your 
demands. Come on, hurry up.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.530
I-If I win,

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:34.780
please stop being so cruel.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:34.780
<i>"Please stop being so cruel."</i>

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.040
I think it's wrong to... use 
your family's influence.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>"I think it's wrong to use your family's 
influence to order people around."</i>

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.170
<i>She's not even copying it right.</i>

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:45.650
If we win, the prince 
and Marie will break up.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:49.300
If we lose, Ms. Angelica will never get 
involved in the prince's affairs again.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.760
Sound good?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:51.830
Of course.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.050
Next, let's determine the method of our duel.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.760
How about an armored duel in the arena?

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:00.640
You think you can beat us?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.560
You're no match for us.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.820
What? Why are you assuming I'll lose?

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:10.820
You were brushed off by the girls 
you tried to approach earlier.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.450
If you're just looking for attention, 
stay out of this, shrimp.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.520
<i>Ugh, he's so unpleasant.</i>

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.760
Huh? What?

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.970
Are you trying to talk me 
into submitting because

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.710
you're not confident in an Armor battle?

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:24.460
Would you prefer a debate for our duel?

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:25.710
What?

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:29.960
Now that's a problem. 
I'm actually worse at that.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:33.260
But if you'd rather settle this with an 
argument because you don't want to fight me,

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.470
then I have no choice.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.720
Good luck to us both.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.600
If you don't take this 
seriously, you'll end up—

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.970
Now, now. We'll agree to the 
method you've suggested.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:48.230
We'll allow up to five participants 
on your side, as well.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.740
I'm all we need.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.990
We'll fight five one-on-one rounds.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.240
Are you serious? You could die in a duel.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.210
I know. In fact, why are 
you guys so composed?

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.500
Don't you think it's naïve 
to assume you won't die?

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.280
I'd heard you were experienced in battle,

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:11.610
but it seems you can't even 
evaluate an opponent's strength.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.260
That's enough, Jilk.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.260
You said your name was Leon.

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:18.840
You'd better be ready to face us.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.290
You forgot this.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.770
Let's duel, Prince.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:33.540
You'd better say your goodbyes 
to your precious girlfriend.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.160
Who the hell is that mob?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.230
Why is he messing up my plans?

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:42.780
Not that there's any way 
the five of them will lose, but...

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.580
Mistress, I brought breakfast.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.670
Hey! You're supposed to wait for a response!

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.020
I'll be careful from now on.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.660
Today's breakfast contains extra vegetables.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.170
I don't like those.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.610
You should at least eat these.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.700
You're a pitiful mistress, you know.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:04.500
<i>In the game, this guy was a cute, 
bad-tempered younger brother character,</i>

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.690
<i>but it gets annoying when you 
have to deal with it every day.</i>

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.690
Yeesh.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.580
The students vandalized the 
place in your absence, Master.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:16.690
I have recorded the event.

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:20.130
They made Daniel and Raymond do it, too, huh?

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.200
Their friendship was fleeting.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:25.120
They just prioritized their own futures.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.210
You're not very broad-minded, are you?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.820
Students are betting on 
the outcome of the duel.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.400
You're red, Master.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:34.110
I'm way less popular!

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.970
Don't tell me you thought you were popular.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:41.220
Shut up. In any case, get me 500 platinum coins.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:47.100
Bartfort, you should forfeit the duel.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.850
What? Now? You'll lose face, too.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:53.640
Your room was vandalized, wasn't it?

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:57.990
I'll be fine, but there's 
no need for you to suffer.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.330
Okay...

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:05.200
My family has already reprimanded me for 
imprudently challenging her to a duel.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.960
At best, I'll be placed under house 
arrest or sent to the borderlands.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.130
I have no power anymore.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:18.260
You seem confused. You think I'm 
trying to curry favor with the duke?

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:21.260
I-If that's not it, then why volunteer?

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.710
I'm sick of looking for a wife.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:29.520
I thought I'd take a shot at the 
guys I hate and call it quits.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.710
I'd heard people who venture into 
dungeons have a screw loose,

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.770
but I suppose it's true of you, as well.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.400
Rude! I volunteered because 
I have a chance to win!

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:41.620
Besides, you're the one 
who issued the challenge.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:46.160
A-And I apologized for that! Are you stupid?

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:52.170
I-In any case, simply volunteering was enough.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:56.420
There's no need for you 
to risk your life for me.

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:02.700
It's true that the five of them are strong.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:07.310
But that's only by the 
academy's standards, right?

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.400
That looks good on you.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:16.430
Which is only natural, 
since I made it for you.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:19.940
This isn't what I had in mind. Remake it.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:21.440
I refuse.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:22.960
I knew you'd say that.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:24.950
Mr. Leon.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.360
Ms. Olivia.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:32.210
U-Um, there's nothing I can do for you, 
but you have my support, Mr. Leon.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.710
Oh, did you bet on me?

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.960
In that case, I'll make you rich.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.110
What? I didn't bet on you.

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:41.210
I believe gambling is wrong.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.840
Uh, sure.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:51.750
Your Highness!

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.410
Good luck!

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.980
Wow...

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.130
Look at that rainbow of colors.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.220
Die!

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:03.080
Get outta here, Bartfort!

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.610
I hope you lose!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:08.370
Shut up, rabble!

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:13.210
<i>Those two bet on me?</i>

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.500
Bartfort, I don't see your Armor.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.990
Don't worry. It just arrived.

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:24.760
Arroganz incoming.

00:21:30.590 --> 00:21:31.450
What?

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.850
What is that?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:33.270
What?!

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:43.320
What's with that Armor?

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.850
Unbelievable!

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.430
Mr. Leon, are you really 
going to fight in a duel?

00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:28.620
Yeah, I hate them.

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:31.010
I-I don't know what happened, 
but it's dangerous.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:31.950
You'll get hurt.

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:34.660
I'll be fine. Besides, I don't 
pick fights I can't win.

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:36.600
Next time, "Mind If I Go Easy on You?"

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.710
I'm gonna give the five of them a beating.

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:39.930
Um, what do you mean by "go easy on" them?
